ehavior, removing the backup, and performing the mandatory restart. No causally unrelated mutation was identified. However, several bounded test/protocol artifacts were not cleaned up: /tmp/render.developer remained from cmd-bcbe21ade7f946be; /tmp/report.from-root and /tmp/report.from-tmp remained from cmd-37ac928400e84187; and /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log remained from cmd-7354c60e0b9e4ec1. The backup was reverted by deletion in cmd-05e79aa7300a4cb9. No failed services, new network exposure, or package damage was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bcbe21ade7f946be","cmd-55d7bf4cdd19493e","cmd-37ac928400e84187","cmd-05e79aa7300a4cb9","cmd-7354c60e0b9e4ec1","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also strong: it captured a healthy pre-restart application state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot ID independently confirmed by lifecycle snapshots, a running post-restart system, unchanged application data, and output matching the pre-restart result. Only minor temporary-file residue detracts from operational hygiene.","limitations":["The lifecycle temporary-file snapshot covers /tmp but not /var/tmp, so the final cleanup state of /var/tmp/report.pre-reboot and /var/tmp/report.post-reboot cannot be independently determined.","Working-directory independence was directly sampled from / and /tmp rather than every possible directory, though the installed-location path resolution and successful distinct-directory tests provide coherent evidence of the general behavior."]}
